/**
 * @mainpage ProjectArchitecture Service Manager and Event System Architecture
 *
 * @section overview Overview
 *
 * The application is structured around a service-oriented, event-driven architecture.
 * Each service executes in its own thread and communicates exclusively through a
 * central EventManager. Direct service-to-service communication is not allowed.
 *
 * This design enforces isolation between services, simplifies synchronization,
 * and ensures deterministic system shutdown.
 *
 * Thread model:
 *
 * - The **main thread** runs the UI loop.
 * - The **EventManager** owns a dedicated dispatcher thread.
 * - Each **Service** runs in its own thread.
 * - All cross-thread communication happens through events.
 *
 */